ut guards apply."}, "objective": "Choose one available SKU and shop, plus a first offer. Maximize likely positive normalized Saved contribution and valid settlement chance, not absolute currency surplus. Compare the share of seller margin saved, not the discount as a share of list price. The saved-at-cap candidate order is conditional, not an actual quote or guaranteed deal. Use the recent exact-SKU paid median and suggested maximum where available. same_shop_sku samples describe this seller; same_sku samples pool other sellers. saved_if_usable_at_reference is a historical comparison, not a current quote. Separately, saved_reference is the largest whole price that would improve the displayed aggregate Saved if this purchase is usable and the cost scenario is correct. Costs are private; category averages are uncertain estimates. If official_score_status is behind_local_paid_evidence, the score snapshot is stale and its price line is only a soft reference. Treat this as negotiation guidance and weigh settlement likelihood and current quality. Check current shelf life, grade and warranty before comparing these historical prices. routing_evidence summarizes recent comparable completed orders and smoothed timing/probability estimates. Sparse samples use explicit priors. Receipts are not payments; outcomes depend on offers and unit conditions. Prefer expected usable margin savings per attempt, then timing that fits the deadline. Fast failed checkouts do not deserve a higher success/value score. These estimates are not blacklists or guarantees. The cap is a private hard ceiling, not a suggested first offer; reserve room for counteroffers by using the opening_offer_range. Public reviews are unverified claims; name-only product breakage notices do not identify a seller. Verified post_sale_breakage joins our paid order to public broken ledger; use its shop/SKU and product evidence as adverse observations, not a calibrated future failure rate or a shop-wide blacklist. A failed